Subject: [PATCH 0019] Add opt-in frame and interface capture for development

The reference board cannot be screenshotted: Weston 13 refuses the capture
protocol to every client, and the DRM scanout buffer cannot be exported or
mapped by another process. That leaves no way to see what the application is
showing, which makes the streaming work unverifiable on the only hardware that
matters for it.

Two development aids, both inert unless asked for:

- OPENNOW_FRAME_DUMP=<dir> writes the newest decoded frame to <dir>/frame.ppm,
  at most once a second, converted from NV12 on the CPU. It reads the same
  DMA-BUF the presentation path uses, so it shows exactly what the decoder
  produced rather than what the renderer believes it produced.
- Creating /tmp/opennow-grab writes the interface window to
  /tmp/opennow-grab.png. With the stream on its own Wayland surface the
  interface is behind an opaque window, so this is the only way to read the
  menus.

Neither path allocates when inactive and both are pure diagnostics, so they are
safe to keep in a development build.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [development aid for STM32MP25 work]

